.SS " Iterable[Tuple[str, Optional[_Encoding], Optional[_Encoding], bool]] bs4\&.builder\&._htmlparser\&.HTMLParserTreeBuilder\&.prepare_markup ( self, _RawMarkup markup, Optional[_Encoding]  user_specified_encoding = \fCNone\fP, Optional[_Encoding]  document_declared_encoding = \fCNone\fP, Optional[_Encodings]  exclude_encodings = \fCNone\fP)"

.PP
.nf
Run any preliminary steps necessary to make incoming markup
acceptable to the parser\&.

:param markup: Some markup -- probably a bytestring\&.
:param user_specified_encoding: The user asked to try this encoding\&.
:param document_declared_encoding: The markup itself claims to be
    in this encoding\&.
:param exclude_encodings: The user asked _not_ to try any of
    these encodings\&.

:yield: A series of 4-tuples: (markup, encoding, declared encoding,
     has undergone character replacement)

    Each 4-tuple represents a strategy for parsing the document\&.
    This TreeBuilder uses Unicode, Dammit to convert the markup
    into Unicode, so the ``markup`` element of the tuple will
    always be a string\&.

.fi
.PP
 
